Carni-Spit

Ingredients: HARDCORE TECHNO / RAVE + K-POP + REBEL, ANGRY & AGGRESSIVE + Bells
Creative Catalyst: It was first performed at a wedding between two rival circus dynasties.

Imagine the precise, militaristic synchronized vocal hooks and glossy perfection of K-pop violently seized by a 190 BPM gabber kick drum, then pulverized by screaming bronze circus bells. Carni-Spit takes the sunny, hyper-curated subversion of modern pop idols and turns it into a riotous, weaponized spit-take. Instead of polished electronic synths, the music relies on brutalist pitch-shifted church chimes, distorted brass carillons, and chaotic 4/4 thunder. Vocals flip on a dime between sweet, autotuned Korean-English "ending fairy" whispers and raw, throat-shredding hardcore screeches, subverting K-pop’s polished elegance into an act of industrial sabotage.

Genre DNA

- Tempo & Pulse: 185–205 BPM. A relentless, bone-shattering gabber four-on-the-floor beat, subverted by sudden, hyper-precise syncopated K-pop dance-break pauses and swing rhythms borrowed from traditional circus marches.
- Harmonic Palette: Minor-key K-pop chord progressions (dorian and harmonic minor) forced through severe, metallic ring modulations, punctuated by dissonant, non-tempered bell overtones.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Micro-Shred Bell Gating: Heavy church bells and brass handbells recorded in high definition, heavily distorted through analog fuzz, and side-chained directly to the kick drum so the metal sounds like it is gasping for air.
  2. Vocal Phase-Splicing: Alternating every syllable of a clean, pitch-corrected girl-group melody with a violently clipped, distorted scream from a megaphone.
  3. The Kinetic Trapeze Drop: An impossible production technique where the high-frequency spectrum (bells and vocals) is Doppler-shifted downward while the sub-bass slides upward, creating a dizzying audio illusion of two sounds passing each other in mid-air at terminal velocity.
- Dynamics: Extreme, binary dynamics. Serene, music-box bell interludes with delicate vocal harmonies get obliterated without warning by 200 BPM distorted kicks and hyper-aggressive crowd shouts.

Scene & Origin Lore

Carni-Spit was forged in the greasepaint and soot of the 2024 unholy matrimony between the scions of the Vane Acrobatics Clan and the Iron-Spoke Freakshow Syndicate. Staged inside a leaking circus tent in a decommissioned rail yard outside Seoul, the wedding turned hostile during the reception when the live K-pop cover act was hijacked by the rival family's sound engineers. Ringmasters plugged high-voltage distortion pedals directly into the venue’s antique tubular bells, driving the crowd into a manic, dust-kicking mosh pit where sequined K-pop idol outfits were torn and reassembled with safety pins and lion-tamer leather. Today, the Carni-Spit scene thrives in clandestine underground tents and abandoned amusement parks. Fashion dictates a collision of high-fashion K-pop aesthetics with carny grime: pastel-dyed hair stiffened with rosin, silk ringmaster coats worn over shredded band tees, heavy face glitter smeared over mock black eyes, and brass circus bells strapped to heavy platform boots so every step rings out like a threat.

Central Instruments & Synths
- Distorted Tubular Bells & Gamelan Gong Chimes: Recorded live, amplified through overdriven tube amps, and used as the primary lead instrument instead of traditional synths.
- Roland TR-909 (Gabber-Modified): Hardcore techno kick drum routed through severe distortion pedals to produce a hollow, square-wave thud.
- Yamaha DX7 (Shattered Preset): Brutal FM synths programmed to emulate metallic glass breaking and metallic carillons.
- Megaphone Vocals: High-clarity vocal mics split into cheap, overdriven bullhorns for instant, hostile texture changes.

For Fans Of: Slayyyter, Atari Teenage Riot, 3TEETH, Stray Kids (at their heaviest), Machine Girl

